<report>
<title>Simple linear regression</title>

<p><b>Equation: </b><in>eq_y</in> <in>eq_x</in></p>

<block name="se">
<p>Standard Error of slope = <inu>slope_err</inu><br />
<ci><in>se_pc</in>% CI for population value of slope = <inu>se_from</inu> to <inu>se_to</inu></ci></p>

<p>Correlation coefficient (r) = <inu>se_r</inu> (r<sub>2</sub> = <inu>se_r2</inu>)</p>

<block name="ci">
<p><ci><in>ci_pc</in>% CI for r (Fisher's z transformed) = <inu>ci_from</inu> to <inu>ci_to</inu></ci></p>

<p>t with <in>df</in> DF = <inu>tdf</inu><br />
<pval>Two sided <inp>p</inp></pval><br />
Power <in>pwr</in></p>

<p><in>sig</in></p>
</block>
</block>
<block name="notcalc">
<p><warn>SE and CI for slope not calculated when r = 1 or -1</warn><br />
<subtotal>Correlation coefficient (r) = <inu>r</inu></subtotal><br />
<warn>CI and t for correlation not calculated when r = 1 or -1</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
